# Canonical Data Package Validation

Command: `python scripts/data_pipeline/validate_data.py` (or `run_pipeline.py` for the full chain). Full machine-readable results: `data/quality/validation_report.json`.

## Result: PASS (39 / 39 checks)

| Area | Result |
|---|---|
| Total `/data` size | 0.12 MB (limit 10 MB) |
| Largest file | `published/intelligence_data.json` 0.07 MB (limit 5 MB) |
| Source sample | 51 rows x 13 columns, 0.009 MB |
| Canonical CSV | 129 rows x 20 columns, 0.031 MB |
| Required columns and order | All 20 present in the mandated order; lowercase snake_case; UTF-8, no BOM |
| `record_id` | Non-null and unique (129) |
| Types and dates | `observed_at` all ISO 8601 (`...T00:00:00Z`); `metric_value` numeric; lat/long blank (not applicable) |
| Flags | `source_name`, `is_synthetic` (all `true`), `data_version` (`1.0.0`) populated on every row |
| Manifest consistency | Counts, column count, sizes, version, synthetic flag, source names and paths all match the files |
| Published JSON | Equals the canonical CSV (129 records) and is regenerated, not hand-edited |
| Reproducibility | Canonical CSV and JSON regenerate byte-identically from the source sample; a clean copy of the repo reproduced every data file byte-for-byte |
| Safety scans | No e-mail addresses, secret patterns, absolute paths or binary files in `/data` |

## Build and deployment readiness
- Existing app files (`frontend/`, `backend/`) are **unchanged**; this post only adds `/data`, `/scripts/data_pipeline`, `/docs`.
- The app does not read `/data` at runtime and needs no live API, so deployment is unaffected. `package.json` was deliberately not given a `prebuild` hook: the frontend Docker build context is `./frontend` and the Node image has no Python.
- Local `npm ci && npm run build` and the Render deploy must be confirmed on your machine (see submission notes); the cloud sandbox used here could not complete `npm ci` (npm crashed) and could not reach the live URL.
</file>

<file path="docs/SAMPLING_AND_REDUCTION_REPORT.md">
# Sampling and Reduction Report

## Original Source
Frontend `mockDatabase` (30 daily rows) + backend synthetic generator (21 rows). Synthetic.

## Original Size
~4.4 KB (about 0.004 MB) of source payload.

## Original Record Count
51 daily source rows (plus 6 node KPI/insight records carried on the frontend rows).

## Original Column Count
13 (flat extract).

## Selected Sampling Method
`full_population_retained` - the population is 0.5% of the 10,000-row limit, so no sampling is applied. A stratified fallback (`sample_data.py`) exists for any future growth; it was tested with a 1,020-row input capped at 300 rows.

## Random Seed
42 (backend generator and the fallback sampler).

## Stratification Fields
source_system x facility x team x status x month (fallback only).

## Date-Coverage Method
All dates kept: 2026-10-24 to 2026-10-28 (frontend) and 2026-10-24 to 2026-10-30 (backend).

## Rare-Record Preservation
All Critical rows kept (Facility A Night Watch plus rare backend Critical days). The fallback guarantees >=1 row per stratum.

## Removed Fields
None from the source sample. Canonical keeps only the 20 mandatory columns; source-specific wide fields become metric rows.

## Removed Records
0. (Interpolated 30-day/YTD display series were never extracted - see inventory.)

## Text Truncation
`text_value` capped at 500 characters; longest insight text is under 100, nothing truncated.

## Sensitive-Data Removal
None needed; the scan (e-mail, secret and absolute-path patterns) found nothing.

## Final Source Sample
- Path: `data/source-sample/source_sample.csv`
- Size: 0.0088 MB
- Record count: 51
- Column count: 13

## Representativeness Checks
Distinct sources, facilities, teams, statuses and dates are identical before and after (see `data/quality/sampling_report.md`).

## Known Sampling Limitations
Not a sample of any real process; it is the complete synthetic population. Conclusions from it are demonstrations only.

## Reproduction Command
`python scripts/data_pipeline/run_pipeline.py`
</file>

